<title>USA: Zitel to post acquisition-related charge.</title>
<headline>Zitel to post acquisition-related charge.</headline>
<dateline>FREMONT, Calif. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zitel Corp said it expects to post a one-time, after-tax charge of about $4.8 million, or $0.31 per share, to write-off acquired in-process research and development.</p>
<p>The charge is related to its previously-announced acquisition of Datametrics Systems Corp, Palmer &amp; Webb Systems Ltd and Palmer &amp; Webb Systems BV, which closed on Monday.</p>
<p>It acquired the three privately held companies for about $12.5 million.</p>
<p>Zitel is an information technology company that specializes in advanced memory algorithms, systems optimization and modeling and search technology.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
